proof = "Current MovePlan preparation traverses CustodySigner::sign_in_scope and EnvelopeKms; the durable outbox holds those exact verified EIP-1559 bytes. Both plan legs are decoded and compared against their original bank calls, and their exact hashes reach the real relay client and committed receipt consumer. The existing intent adapter verifies and enqueues its actual custody transaction instead of signing a replacement."

[finding.native-approval-clock-units]
policy_recipient_repair = "At 1afafd10fceea00834273cdd310d171322287289, cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1, private /out/logs/verify-1.log: producer passed and approval reached NativeEffectApprovalCarrier::bind, where evaluate_local refused because the fixture Transfer policy named raw recipient public-key bytes instead of the canonical account ID used by both the compiled intent and signed consent. The fixture policy now derives that same recipient account ID through account_id_for_protocol at protocol version 3; amount 10, required approval, fee bounds and every regression assertion are retained. Final qualification belongs to the hf-build/hf-done ledger."
commit_coverage = "The retained bootstrap peer produces and verifies a signed checkpoint for every height from 1 through HEAD plus its required successor, using the recorded px_getCommit chain 125 and validator set. Each successor links the previous verified header hash, and all native result sets are complete and empty. The clock regression can read heights 63, 62 and 61 at HEAD 64 and authenticate the admitted history window; an unknown commit height returns JSON-RPC commit not found instead of panicking in the peer. Regression expectations remain unchanged; only the final hf-build/hf-done ledger records executed qualification."
rate_window_qualification_repair = "At b898f10a04565c09afc5296fd692c132e7b1faae, cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1, private /out/logs/verify-2.log: the producer passed, while approval history requested commit height 61. unsigned_access forwards rate_window_ms unchanged into TimedCapability.rate_ceilings, which the daemon consumes as seconds; this continuation records that existing unit mismatch without changing its behavior or the consent. The fixture adds a production-generated, validator-signed predecessor 60001 seconds before the head so authenticated history covers the entire admitted 60000-second window with complete result sets and linked successors. The final hf-build/hf-done ledger alone records qualification."
history_qualification_repair = "At 615cc2b4898ae0bd495aec8453ad98afa8e4cfb2, cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1, private /out/logs/verify-1.log: native_producer_clock_units passed and native approval reached opcode 67, whose authenticated 60-second policy-history read requested commit height 62 absent from the fixture. native_send_history_commits now produces the additional validator-signed predecessor at HEAD minus 2, 61 seconds before the head, using the production checkpoint, vote-signing and commit-verification paths. Its linked successors and complete empty block_results authenticate the entire rate window without changing any policy or assertion. Final executed qualification remains in the hf-build/hf-done ledger."
preflight_compile_repair = "At 27c89cb8c771d613145f0cc983023cd6df846eaf, cargo build --locked --manifest-path services/human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-human-service --test repair_22_33_63 exited 101, private /out/logs/build-1.log: the integration preflight cannot call HumanOwnerNativeSessionV1::credential because it is crate-private. The preflight now uses fixture.credential.token_id(), the public production session credential used to construct that same retained session; no credential visibility or validation changes."
encoder_contract = "The Journey request preserves CompiledIntent::payload_hash from layerx_wire::hash::payload_hash_for, SHA256(LXP/v1/payload-hash followed by NUL and the exact canonical payload). The approval preflight asserts that the registry-bound compiled payload bytes and payload_hash_for commitment equal engine_request.payload and payload_hash. encode_native_send_prepare_v2 at server/native_send.rs forwards that commitment without comparing it to raw SHA256, retaining every other request, signed-purpose and local-grant check; it holds no registry. The production daemon reconstructs the payload against its module registry and verifies payload_hash_for in native_send_preview_authorization before admission. The real admission, retained approval decision and resume remain required; execution evidence remains solely in the hf-build/hf-done ledger."
admission_preflight = "The approval case repeats the production preview with the exact Journey request (quoted fee, hex action idempotency key and plan timestamps), compares all 18 purpose fields with individual difference diagnostics, and compares canonical bytes, preimage and owner key. Before engine advance it obtains a production custody SendPurpose grant, checks its signer and disclosure, verifies its Ed25519 signature against the quoted consent key, and requires the production V2 prepare encoder, EnvelopeCredential and envelope encoder to accept. Each preflight refusal names its stage; no daemon check is changed. Final executed gate evidence belongs to the hf-build/hf-done ledger."
sender_binding = "The approval case explicitly binds fixture.account.evm_address() through AgentBoundary::bind_transaction_sender before binding the native journey context, both initially and after reopening. It admits the signed owner assertion before asserting that custody.evm_wallet and the real production preview purpose name that same sender. Journey failure diagnostics retain the phase, stored native purpose, custody refusal and transport response to distinguish the already validated signed grant, sender, current owner and prepared transaction stages from later approval admission. No runtime refusal check changes."
sender_qualification_repair = "At 7c218fdfa171661c785cf2645931b9814db06888 the declared build passed, but cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1, private /out/logs/verify-1.log: native_producer_clock_units passed and the new approval custody wallet assertion required owner admission after authorize_access consumed its signing assertion. The case now admits that same signed owner assertion before the production wallet read; no assertion is removed or relaxed. Final evidence remains in the hf-build/hf-done ledger."
qualification_repair = "At c7d1cbf0b31c041bca442cc033de8e10401fbab7, cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1, private /out/logs/verify-1.log: the Journey preview reached opcode 66 but its exact transaction fee differed from the arbitrary plan fee. The approval plan now obtains its exact fee from a production preview and retains every fee equality check; its later purpose must equal the quoted purpose. Final qualification remains owned by the hf-build/hf-done ledger."
status = "implemented_not_qualified"
observed = "At candidate 2a576ffaefeb68212ed132f9594492a1947f9891, cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1; private /out/logs/verify-1.log records native_approval_clock_units failing in JourneyEngine::advance with Agent(Refused), before any opcode 66 request. The same candidate passed cargo build --locked --manifest-path services/human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-human-service --test repair_22_33_63, exit 0, private /out/logs/build-1.log."
refused_path = "JourneyEngine::advance_native -> AgentRuntime::native_journey_preview -> native_send_preview_v2 at src/server/agent_runtime.rs:5416 converts NativeLocalGrantConsentV1.signature ([u8; 64], layerx-agent-api/src/identity.rs:550) into &[u8; 65], then maps the impossible conversion to AgentBoundaryError::Refused before exchange. This is not AgentFailure::Refused from agents/create.rs, and no signed lifecycle request or receipt was requested; no lifecycle binding check may be bypassed to repair this earlier production interface."
runtime_repair = "services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/src/server/agent_runtime.rs::native_send_preview_v2 writes NativeLocalGrantConsentV1.signature directly as its declared [u8; 64], matching the daemon NATIVE_SEND_OWNER_PREVIEW_V1 reader.fixed(). The regression asserts the 64-byte signed consent and exercises production decoding before approval admission and resume."
daemon_decoder = "services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human.rs decodes opcode 66 (NATIVE_SEND_OWNER_PREVIEW_V1) into NativeLocalGrantConsentV1.signature via reader.fixed(), whose inferred array type is [u8; 64]; this handler already matches the shared API and needs no signature-size change. No daemon file is changed."
transport = "The retained client fixture accepts on its own worker until Peer is dropped and loops production serve_one over every frame of each accepted pooled connection until EOF, then accepts the next connection. Teardown shuts down the active socket before joining the worker. ObservedTransport delegates unchanged frames to AcceptedTransport and retains the request opcode, production refusal reason and native envelope HTTP errors for assertion messages. The Journey advance assertion names the actual 64-byte grant and daemon NATIVE_SEND_OWNER_PREVIEW_V1 path. The selected native Journey path uses preview/admit/resume, not AgentCreationContract lifecycle submission; no substitute lifecycle evidence is supplied or check changed. The final hf-build/hf-done ledger qualifies this continuation, not the historical observed failure above."
test = "repair_22_33_63::native_approval_clock_units"
source_test = "clock_regressions::approval; native_journey_approval::genuine_native_journey_holds_reopens_and_resumes_original_authority"
peer_request = "NativeOwnerContextV1 (Human frame opcode 64), issued by authorize_access before local consent signing; the fixture delegates this request to UnifiedAgentOwner::native_owner_context_v1 and asserts its owner, generation, signed expiry and millisecond protocol time. Node RPC and authority read diagnostics identify any unavailable producer dependency in the private gate log."
custody_request = "The fixture verifies that its retained human-primary descriptor is HumanPrimary with the scope owner's public key, constructs the grant with production unsigned_access, validates its millisecond lifetime and binds real WebAuthn step-up evidence to its exact digest and SecuritySettings operation. A mandatory sign_native_consent_in_scope call exposes the typed provider refusal before authorize_access masks it; successful signing must verify against the owner key, and authorize_access uses a fresh subsequent step-up ceremony."
limitation = "The clock fixtures select the production AttestorKms::connect_with_clock provider and Keystore::open_production, not EnvelopeKms, whose default sign_native refuses. The provider enrolls human-primary through create_owned_key and signs over mutual TLS with public deterministic signing keys; the local peers validate production native grant/purpose encodings, owner assertions, signer membership and exact session replay. This exercises the service provider and client, not a deployed threshold quorum; the hf-build/hf-done ledger is the sole evidence of executed gates."
proof = "The distinct public-key approval scenario calls production authorize_access, JourneyEngine::start_native and advance, requires AwaitingApproval, drops the principal store and runtime, reloads the retained journey and consent, and calls native_effect_approval_decide and the production resume path. Assertions retain the action, consent, canonical digest, approval binding and Granted/Prepared outcome; seconds reach session/Journey APIs and milliseconds reach purpose expiry checks before, at and after signed expiry. Positive native custody and approval assertions remain mandatory; only the task gate ledger can qualify this path."

[finding.native-producer-clock-units]
qualification_repair = "At c7d1cbf0b31c041bca442cc033de8e10401fbab7, cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1, private /out/logs/verify-1.log: preview and reopen succeeded, then assert_expiry passed signed consent to the pre-signing NativeConsent validator, which requires a zero signature. The expiry helper now verifies the actual signed grant cryptographically and validates its unsigned signing material before, at and after the same signed expiry; stored consent and all expiry assertions remain intact."
status = "implemented_not_qualified"
observed = "At candidate 2a576ffaefeb68212ed132f9594492a1947f9891, cg spec done 18.1747.1 -f layerx-merge --root /work/paxeer-monorepo exited 1; private /out/logs/verify-1.log records native_producer_clock_units failing in its first preview_send_v2 with Unavailable after opcode 13. The same candidate passed the declared build, exit 0, private /out/logs/build-1.log. These are observed failures, not qualification claims; the final ledger owns later gate results."
refused_path = "preview_send_v2 -> load_access -> AgentRuntime::pending_nonce at src/server/agent_runtime.rs:1931 reads u64 plus rung, while production ProductionHumanOperations::account_sequence at layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs:15690 emits only u64. Reader::u8 returns CorruptResponse at the missing byte; load_access erases it to AgentFailure::Unavailable at src/server/native_send.rs:505. The worker remains listening and answers each real request; adding a synthetic rung or replacing load_access would bypass the broken interface."
runtime_repair = "services/human/crates/layerx-human-service/src/server/agent_runtime.rs::pending_nonce reads only the u64 ACCOUNT_SEQUENCE field and finishes the response; account_state retains its separate rung layout. native_send_preview_v2 writes the 64-byte local-grant signature directly. Both cases assert the real daemon ACCOUNT_SEQUENCE response size and the grant signature size without rewriting frames."
transport = "NativeOwnerContextV1 opcode 64, pending_nonce, NativeSendOwnerPreviewV1 opcode 66 and NativeSendEnvelopeV1 opcode 67 share the case-lifetime listener. Each accepted pooled connection loops serve_one with the same production owner until EOF before the listener accepts another connection. The V2 preview assertion retains the actual response opcode, payload size and production refusal text, including the observed account-sequence shape when load_access erases CorruptResponse to Unavailable; responses are never rewritten. The final hf-build/hf-done ledger qualifies this continuation, not the historical observed failure above."
test = "repair_22_33_63::native_producer_clock_units"
source_test = "clock_regressions::producer; native_send_producer::genuine_human_owner_session_consent_preview_and_reopen"
peer_request = "The producer scenario also obtains NativeOwnerContextV1 through the real Unix transport before authorize_access, then uses NativeSendOwnerPreviewV1 for preview_send_v2; the existing hf-build/hf-done ledger is the sole qualification evidence reference."
custody_request = "The independent producer key traverses the same production grant encoding, owner/lifetime validation, authenticated SecuritySettings binding and mandatory native custody signature verification before authorize_access and V2 preview; it has its own principal and retained store."
limitation = "The independent producer uses the same production AttestorKms native-signing path, its own deterministic key and scoped keystore, with a fresh admitted signed owner assertion before each consumed signing request. A public TLS identity authenticates all three local protocol peers; the Send V2 signing request also resolves the held wallet identity and checks its real secp256k1 public key and sender. RuntimeClock uses the fixture clock for native replay retention. This focused regression does not qualify deployed threshold infrastructure, protected fixtures or unrelated rotation findings; no success is inferred from a build."
proof = "The separate public-key producer scenario obtains owner consent through authorize_access with real WebAuthn step-up and custody, verifies its signature, and calls preview_send_v2 through AgentRuntime and the production daemon owner before and after PrincipalStore reopen. Assertions compare canonical bytes, signing preimage, complete V2 purpose, consent bytes, sender, key and action, accept before signed expiry and refuse at and after it. Offline protocol inputs use the daemon regression's production ABI/checkpoint encoders and an embedded Anvil recording; no approval facts or journey phases are manufactured. Positive native custody and preview assertions remain mandatory; no unrun qualification is claimed."

